description:
Sets two or three books side by side and shows them as a comparison grid. Aspects: "difficulty" (overall and per-dimension scores, and each book's hardest and easiest dimensions), "themes" (shared and distinct), "length" (word count and reading time), "style" (primary genre and literary regard) and "awards".

Use when the user asks to compare specific books, which of them is harder or longer, or which to read first. For a single book, use get_book_details. To find books, use search_books.

Default aspects: difficulty, themes, length.

Examples:
- {"book_ids": ["crime-and-punishment", "the-brothers-karamazov"]}
- {"book_ids": ["1984", "brave-new-world", "fahrenheit-451"], "aspects": ["themes", "difficulty"]}
